{
  "$comment": [
    "Issue #601 — keys whose translated value is DELIBERATELY identical to the",
    "English reference. `scripts/i18n-validate.mjs` treats an identical value as",
    "an ERROR unless the key is listed here, so this file is what lets the gate",
    "be hard instead of a warning nobody reads.",
    "",
    "Every entry carries a reason code. Adding a key here is a decision, and the",
    "reason is what makes it reviewable — 'it looked fine' is not one.",
    "",
    "  brand        — a product or company name (omadia, Palaia, Postgres,",
    "                 Anthropic). Translating it would be wrong, not incomplete.",
    "  glossary     — an omadia domain term kept English on purpose. See",
    "                 GLOSSARY.md for the term and the reasoning.",
    "  loanword     — the German word IS the English word ('optional', 'live',",
    "                 'Filter', 'max. 50 MB'). Nothing to translate.",
    "  placeholder  — example input shown in a form field. It illustrates a",
    "                 FORMAT; localising it would teach the user a wrong value.",
    "  code         — a literal command, type signature, or code fragment. It is",
    "                 copied and executed verbatim.",
    "  diagnostic   — a raw field/flag name echoed from the API for support",
    "                 purposes. It must match what the logs and the API say, or",
    "                 it stops being useful for diagnosis."
  ],
